-- Step 21: credit notes and sales returns.
-- track: A
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / ALTER TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/*/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- A credit note is a sales document of its own kind. It is made from one posted sales invoice
-- and takes back part of it: each of its lines is a line of that invoice, for no more than is
-- left of what was invoiced, and says how much of what came back is damaged. The app writes the
-- draft; it is posted once, by a function of the database's own, which checks every figure
-- against the invoice, takes the CN number and posts one journal:
--
--   debit   Sales                                   the value of the goods taken back, before tax
--   debit   Sales tax payable (output tax)          the sales tax on them, and any extra tax
--   debit   Further tax payable                     the further tax on them
--   credit  Trade receivables (the customer)        as much as is still unpaid of the invoice
--   credit  Advances from customers (the same)      the rest: the customer's credit
--
--   debit   Stock in trade                          goods that can be sold again, back on the
--                                                   shelf at the cost they left at
--   debit   Stock adjustments                       damaged goods, written off at once
--   credit  Cost of goods sold                      the cost of everything that came back
--
-- Credit left over is set against other invoices later, each with a journal that moves the
-- amount from advances to the customer's account. A posted credit note is never cancelled.
--
-- What already existed and is written out again here, wider, with nothing taken away (the
-- founder's yes, 2026-11-14):
--   the policy sales_documents_insert              a credit note may be written, by the owner,
--                                                  an accountant or the sales manager
--   app.check_sales_document()                     what a credit note is made from, that only
--                                                  its own function posts it, its CN number
--   app.check_sales_document_part()                what a line of a credit note is
--   app.receivable_items(uuid, uuid)               what is still unpaid on an invoice now also
--                                                  takes off what credit notes settled of it
-- The two guards are those of drizzle/0018_sales_invoices.sql with only the lines a credit note
-- needs added; for every other kind of document they do what they did.
--
-- Every function here searches pg_catalog first and the temporary schema last, never an empty
-- path (drizzle/0023_safe_search_path.sql says why); the rules written out again keep that.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE100 to SE199 (docs/PARALLEL.md); Step 32 used
-- SE100 to SE111, some of which mean the same here (SE102, SE108, SE111):
--   SE112  no such credit note in this company (or outside the member's branches)
--   SE113  a credit note is made from a posted sales invoice: for its customer, into its
--          warehouse, on or after its date
--   SE114  more is being returned than is left of what was invoiced
--   SE115  the credit note's figures are not those of its invoice
--   SE116  a posted credit note is never cancelled
--   SE117  a credit note is posted only by the database's own posting function
--   SE118  more than is left of the credit
--   SE119  opening balances that credit has been set against are not reversed (and SE056 for
--          reversing any opening balances outside a read committed transaction)
--   SE120  a line of a credit note is a line of its invoice, in everything but how much
--   SE121  the invoice has no record of the goods leaving stock

-- ── generated by drizzle-kit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

